  "package_isolation": [
    "The original three tests each reached a real public-installation checkpoint and failed because the unaudited final directory was visible before publication. The host then aborted while initiating panic; no failed-test summary is invented.",
    "Real temporary directories, secure recursive copy, manifest parsing and identity validation are used. The test checkpoint observes or mutates actual files; it does not replace those operations.",
    "Only a fully audited package is moved into its final path by a same-filesystem no-replace directory publication. A competing empty directory survives unchanged.",
    "A complete metadata sidecar is published through an exclusive hard link before the package becomes discoverable. Existing records are never overwritten; a failed package publication removes its own sidecar.",
    "Concurrent real installers for the same identity produce exactly one success and one rejection, without mixed bytes or leftover transaction state.",
    "Rejected invalid, changed or reselected staged manifests leave no package, metadata or temporary transaction contents. Source package bytes remain unchanged.",
    "Every audited skills, MCP, Hooks, Apps, onboarding and interface resource path is rebased to the final root and matches a fresh real manifest load; marketplace provenance is visible through discovery.",
    "Nested installation roots are rejected before creating directories in the source. Source symlinks are not followed, external file bytes are untouched and package shell commands are not executed."
  ],
  "security_differences": [
    "Unlike upstream update replacement, this entry point refuses every existing final directory or metadata entry, including empty directories and symlinks.",
    "No upstream command migration or generated manifest injection is performed; source and installed package bytes are not rewritten.",
    "On macOS publication uses renamex_np(RENAME_EXCL); Linux uses renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE) through the existing libc dependency; Windows uses directory rename which refuses an existing directory. A kernel or filesystem rejecting the required operation fails closed without overwrite fallback.",
    "Package and provenance entries have separate filesystem names. Provenance is complete before package publication, so discovery cannot see a half-copied package; this does not claim a multi-entry filesystem transaction or SIGKILL recovery.",
    "A pre-existing install-root container may remain empty after a rejected copy as before; owned package, provenance and staging entries are removed. Persistent installation-state recovery belongs to task 51."
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "An additional real discovery checkpoint proved staging could masquerade as a plugin for a pre-existing permitted local name. A fixed intermediate payload directory now prevents staging from entering discovery; the final 12-test run includes that regression.",
    "The first green compilation was deliberately interrupted by this agent before tests to fix source mutation for a nested install root. Only its own Cargo group was stopped, its lease was released, and no behavior evidence was claimed."
  ],
